Changelog: 27-11-2026 23:15:51

Fixed. After a failed combined test, a level the healthy WGPs never reached says "Not healthy" again. It said
"Failed together", which read as if that level had been tested (a board, 27-11-2026: 40 CUs after a test of 38).
The old write is confirmed on that board: 38 CUs passed the combined test, were installed and came up at boot.

Changelog: 27-11-2026 22:49:57

Fixed. The test's GPU load runs with a small VRAM split too. The load's size was three quarters of the VRAM, which is
384 MiB with a 512 MB split, and memtest_vulkan refuses that. The test then ended as LOAD-FAIL although nothing was
wrong with the CUs (a board, 27-11-2026). The size is now at least 1024 MiB when the memory is there.

Changelog: 27-11-2026 22:07:43

Fixed. The CU unlock is written the old way again: `CC_GC_SHADER_ARRAY_CONFIG` cleared, each row's mask in
`SPI_PG_ENABLE_STATIC_WGP_MASK`, and the union of the rows in `RLC_PG_ALWAYS_ON_WGP_MASK`. That is the write every
boot unlock used until 27-11-2026. The write of that day set CC to the mask's inverse and left RLC alone. It was
tested live but never at boot. On 27-11-2026 a boot unlock of 38 CUs written that way hung the GPU two seconds after
the login screen started, on a board whose live test of the same mask had passed. Do not install a boot unlock with
the two releases that carry that write. `--writes` defaults to `cc,spi,rlc` again. The wiki's register table says so
again. A test now keeps the other write out.

Changelog: 27-11-2026 20:55:57

Added. Step 4 offers every count above the highest even level, up to all healthy WGPs, each with the rows that give
it the most speed. On a board with one failing WGP that is 34, 36 and 38 CUs. A count that runs slower than its number
says what it runs like, such as "Like 36 CUs" for 38. Before, only the counts that add speed were shown, so 34 and 38
were missing (owner, 27-11-2026).

Changelog: 27-11-2026 19:59:41

Release 1.1.0.

Changelog: 27-11-2026 16:16:03

Added. CU Unlock applies and keeps counts with uneven rows. Step 4 offers the counts above the highest even level
that add speed, such as 36 CUs with 4, 5, 4 and 5 WGPs on the rows, as pills. Each is tested as a whole and installed
like a level. `ps5-cu-unlock.sh` and the gate accept every mask with 3, 4 or 5 WGPs on every row. Before, only
24, 32 and 40 CUs could be installed.
A wrong fact is corrected. The scripts, the window and the wiki said that an uneven mask runs as fast as its smallest
row. A board measured otherwise with vkpeak on 27-11-2026. The two shader engines, SE0 and SE1, run in step, and a
mask runs like 4 CUs for each WGP in its smaller engine. So 28 CUs with 7 WGPs in each engine scored 17 percent over
24 CUs, and 28 CUs with 8 and 6 scored the same as 24. The scripts say what a mask runs like when that is less than
its count. The wiki's CU Unlock chapter has the measured scores as a table.
The summary of the test script says "The even version:" where it said "Use the even version instead:".

Changelog: 27-11-2026 07:31:39

Fixed. The CU unlock no longer lists a WGP as active that its mask leaves off. Before, it cleared
CC_GC_SHADER_ARRAY_CONFIG on every row, which listed all 5 WGPs as active. That included a WGP that failed its test.
It also wrote the always-on mask as the union of the rows, for all rows at once. Now CC_GC_SHADER_ARRAY_CONFIG marks
every WGP that the row's mask leaves off as inactive, as the chip does at stock. RLC_PG_ALWAYS_ON_WGP_MASK is not
written anymore. Both ps5-cu-unlock.sh and ps5-cu-bisect.sh write this way. --writes defaults to cc,spi, and rlc
still writes the union on request. The script's check for an unlock that is on since boot looked for CC values of 0.
A board that reads the upper bits as 1 never matched. The check now reads bits 16-20, and also sees the boot
service. The wiki's register table said CC is cleared to 0 and the always-on mask is the union. It now says what is
written. tests/test_unlock_writes.py covers the writes.

Changelog: 26-11-2026 20:34:55

Fixed. The mouse wheel changes a list, a number field or a slider only after a click on it. Before, a wheel
turn over a window changed every value the pointer passed. Until the click, the wheel scrolls the page under it.
WheelGuard in widgets.py is a copy of core's.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 17:44:44

Release 1.0.1.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 15:16:11

Fixed. memtest_vulkan wrote its own memtest_vulkan.log into the folder the script was started from. It now runs in
the script's logs folder, which --reset removes.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 13:15:49

Release 1.0.0.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 12:57:36

Fixed. ps5-cu-bisect.sh measured a GPU load of 0% on systems whose awk is mawk, as on Debian and Ubuntu. mawk wrote
large engine times as 5e+09, which bash can't count with. The script now writes them as whole numbers. Bazzite's awk
is gawk, which wasn't affected. The load test failed in the local CI's Debian container for this reason.

Fixed. The load reading was also wrong at random where the locale writes numbers with a decimal comma, as nl_NL does.
The script's timer then read only the microseconds. It now reads the time with a point or a comma. The load test also
runs in such a locale where one is installed.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 12:21:30

Breaking. The app is now called PS5 CU Unlock, before PS5 CU Tools. The app key compute, its folder and file names
stay. The bottom row no longer has the label Other actions, and its pills start at the left. Show details and Show
advanced are now the pills Details and Advanced at the right end of that row. Under the name they say Show or Hide.
The window always opens 900 pixels wide, also when it was wider before. It fits its height to the page once it shows,
so a first window no longer cuts half of the page off. The tooltips are rounded boxes on the window's dark background,
as in the suite's other apps. The wiki's picture of the window shows the new row.

Changelog: 24-11-2026 04:05:33

Fixed. Install no longer writes the masks to the GPU while the desktop runs, because that can freeze the board.
ps5-cu-unlock.sh --install only saves the masks and turns on the boot service. The unlock turns on at the next restart.
ps5-cu-bisect.sh measures the GPU load from each program's gfx and compute time in /proc/<pid>/fdinfo when the kernel
can't fill gpu_busy_percent. The results then no longer say "GPU load only reached 0%".

Added. The window runs the CU test itself, in four steps, and no terminal opens anymore. The steps are rows at the top.
Each row says what came out of it or the one thing to do now, with its pill on the row. The steps are Scan, Safety
check, Test each WGP, and Choose and install. A CU map shows every WGP's state and each row's mask. By default every
attempt runs in one boot. With Same boot off, the window restarts the board after each attempt and opens again after
the login. The board doesn't go to sleep during a test, and a notification says when the test ends. When everything
is done, a green bar says that you're finished.

